{"id":7303,"date":"2022-08-09T11:52:17","date_gmt":"2022-08-09T11:52:17","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=student&#038;p=7303"},"modified":"2022-08-09T11:52:20","modified_gmt":"2022-08-09T11:52:20","slug":"dr-noreldin-osman-adam-ibrahim","status":"publish","type":"student","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student\/dr-noreldin-osman-adam-ibrahim\/","title":{"rendered":"Dr. Noreldin Osman Adam Ibrahim"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim profile-banner bg-alt\" style=\"background-color:none\"><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Dr. Noreldin Osman Adam Ibrahim<\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"primary-bold profile-position prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Sudan<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Postdoctoral Researcher &#8211; University of KwaZulu Natal<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Osman.jpeg\"\/>\n\n<p class=\"profile-testimonial invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-success invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-studentbio invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n\n<p>Dr. Osman Noreldin is an independent researcher in fluid dynamics and numerical methods. He completed his PhD in applied mathematics from the University of KwaZulu Natal in 2018. During his PhD, he worked as an Adhoc lecturer in the School of Mathematics, Statistics and Computer Science at the same university which continued from 2017 till 2021.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>From June 2019 to July 2021, Osman also worked as a postdoctoral fellow at the University of KwaZulu Natal, co-supervising three PhD students. One of these three has already been awarded his PhD, with the other two progressing positively on this path.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Osman has authored many articles, twelve of which have been published in reputable journals and conference papers. He has attended and presented at various international and local workshops and conferences and is an active member of the South Africa Mathematical Society.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Dr. Osman Noreldin is an independent researcher in fluid dynamics and numerical methods. He completed his PhD in applied mathematics from the University of KwaZulu Natal in 2018. During his PhD, he worked as an Adhoc lecturer in the School of Mathematics, Statistics and Computer Science at the same university which continued from 2017 till<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":12,"featured_media":7304,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-testimonial":"","profile-success":"","profile-studentbio":"","profile-studentname":"Dr. Noreldin Osman Adam Ibrahim","profile-country":"Sudan","profile-program":"Postdoctoral Researcher - University of KwaZulu Natal"},"tags":[],"student_types":[13],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Osman.jpeg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/joel\/","display_name":"joel"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 3 years ago","modified":"Updated 3 years ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on August 9, 2022","modified":"Updated on August 9, 2022"},"absolute_dates_time":{"created":"Posted on August 9, 2022 11:52 am","modified":"Updated on August 9, 2022 11:52 am"},"featured_img_c